<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies eight issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies eight issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Assurance Corp said it has qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Alvord USD, Calif., $12 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Illinois, $100 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Wadena, Minn., $1.675 million improvement GOs.</p>
<p>--Iredell County, N.C., $22.180 GOs.</p>
<p>--Monroe Township Board of Education, N.J., $15.470 million school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Nassau County, N.Y., $191.185 million general improvement bonds and $3.205 million sewer district bonds.</p>
<p>--Georgetown County, S.C., $6.040 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
